WEBVTT

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.010
So you're Natsu?

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.480
I'd heard rumors, but you 
really do look like him.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.390
This again?

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.060
I thought the other host 
named Natsu already quit.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:18.370
Yeah, but you look just like him from behind.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.370
<i>The other Natsu, huh?</i>

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.370
<i>Since everyone kept saying the same thing...</i>

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.100
<i>At first, I headed out half out of 
curiosity and half because of a hunch.</i>

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.010
I'm hungry. Hey, you want 
to get something to eat?

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.510
Oh, don't worry. I'll pay.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.530
I don't care! Just let me out!

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.640
Who are you, anyway?

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.520
I'd like to ask you the same thing.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:50.520
As far as I know, Haru, Aki, and 
Shima are Kaidou Takashi's only sons.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.030
Who are you?

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.710
I thought I heard Ren's voice just now.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.500
Do you know the Kaidou family?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.420
Uncle Kaidou is my mom's younger brother.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.870
I guess that makes me and Haru cousins.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.510
<i>Cousins...</i>

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.370
<i>He does look a lot like Haru.</i>

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:49.020
I just came to check things out, since I heard 
rumors at work about a man named Natsu.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:53.020
I laughed when I learned that 
honor student Haru became a host.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.500
Well, I guess he couldn't help it.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.530
His parents died in an accident, right?

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.780
It's actually pretty tragic that 
Haru's the only one who survived.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.970
Wait, then when did you...

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.700
I don't feel so good.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.290
Carsick.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.930
What?! Wait!

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.910
Hey, wait!

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.290
I-I'm going to puke.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.170
<i>There's the Haru I don't know 
who's supposedly this man's cousin,</i>

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.330
<i>and the Haru I don't know 
who's an honor student.</i>

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.600
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:30.180
<i>I don't even know where the 
Kaidou family gravesite is.</i>

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.190
Go to hell!

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.690
You suck, idiot!

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.200
Hey, you.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.410
You should've told me sooner 
that you were going to throw up.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.450
You covered my car in puke.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.670
You're the one who forced me to get in.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.560
And you're a reckless driver.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.460
Shut up.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.960
I washed your clothes for you.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.530
I'd better get to work.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.720
Once your clothes are dry, 
call someone to come pick you up.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.480
Is this place haunted by ghosts?

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.470
No.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.860
It's a love letter from my recent ex.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.480
I hope you get cursed.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.230
That's harsh. You don't even know me.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.870
You don't know me, either.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.490
True...

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.630
I only know you're the youngest Kaidou brother 
and you lived in Canada until last year.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:29.490
Natsu and his love for his brothers 
is famous among other hosts.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.750
I had a hunch it was him ever since I heard there 
was a man named Natsu who looked like me.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.750
He's as big a liar as ever, isn't he?

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:41.010
That's what usually happens when 
you try to be nice to people.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.590
What's your name?

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:46.760
Ren.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.900
Okay, Ren, here's the key to 
this place. You can keep it.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.270
And here's my card.

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:54.260
Do you have a cell phone?

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.270
I don't have it with me today.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.260
Then give me your number. 
You can do that, right?

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.490
After all, we're cousins.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:02.500
Fine.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.200
And...

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.780
There's more?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.780
Don't tell your brothers you met me.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:09.880
Why not?

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.310
There's some stuff going on 
between my dad and Uncle Kaidou.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.040
Anyway, see you later.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.300
Hello, Mikiko?

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.800
Thanks for coming to pick me up.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.000
You're welcome.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.100
I was so surprised when you 
called saying you were lost.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.060
About today...

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.390
I know. I won't tell Haru about it.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.270
Or why you're working.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:40.810
Thanks.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.090
Now hurry up.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:46.760
When I called Haru earlier, 
he said he was waiting to eat dinner.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:47.320
Okay.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.930
See you later, Ren.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:55.580
It's me. There's something 
I want you to look into.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.330
Ren, you're late!

00:05:58.930 --> 00:05:59.920
Welcome home.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:00.830
Ren...

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.530
Mikiko called to say I'd be late.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.840
Then you should keep your phone on.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:10.840
Our eldest brother over there
hasn't shut up about it.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.290
Sorry I'm late.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.440
It's fine. You must be hungry.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.970
Did you go to see Mikiko-san today?

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:18.600
Yeah.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.820
Oh, Ren. Old Man Onodera called.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:27.110
He said not to come to work tomorrow, 
and that you'll start back up on Monday.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.390
Got it.

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:31.000
He said you found the corpse of an animal?

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.370
What?! Are you sure that room's safe?

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.400
His pet dog died.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.500
Did you know there was a dog living there?

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.520
How would I know?

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:43.850
I wasn't interested in the 
other residents, and anyway...

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.740
Oh, damn it! This is such a pain!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:46.260
Haru?

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.790
Ren, you should quit working for the old man.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:50.760
Why?

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:55.000
Not only is the room full of garbage, 
but you even found a dead dog.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.380
No matter how you look at it,
it's not a decent job.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.060
I'll tell the old man you're quitting.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.270
You can't just decide that!

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:06.210
If you want money, help around 
the café. I'll pay you.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.780
If there's anything I can do here, I'll help.

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.580
But you don't need to pay me for that,

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.360
and I won't quit working for Gramps.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.790
I'm going to keep cleaning the 
apartment until we're finished.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:19.880
Hey, Ren... What about dinner?

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:20.790
I'll eat it later!

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.250
What was that?

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:24.810
Is he going through a rebellious phase?

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.340
No, rebellious phases are more irrational.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.550
Ren's logic makes sense.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.760
Are you saying I'm the irrational one?

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.060
I understand your concern, 
but Ren's not wrong.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.220
Let him do what he wants.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.770
That job will be done in another week, anyway.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:45.710
If you guys say so.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.250
Man, I'm so bored!

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:52.280
I thought Ren would be with me 
all day during his summer vacation!

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:58.510
Oh, right... The key...

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:03.290
Shiba Natsuo?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.290
Oh, man...

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.290
That kid wore me out today.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:10.520
I shouldn't have tried to butt in.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.240
Has the cleaning fairy been here?

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.430
Buy new curtains.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.680
Uh, good morning.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.440
Kiri-chan?

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.460
Ren's in the house.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:30.650
Actually, I'm here to talk to you today.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:31.190
Me?

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.700
It's about this.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.300
Ren.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:39.120
I'm almost finished handpicking the beans.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.580
Is there anything else I can do?

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.200
No.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:43.890
But take a look at this.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.830
I heard you dropped it in the lake 
when Lyuba jumped on you.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.290
A park employee fished it 
out of the lake for you.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.290
Kiri-chan just brought it to me.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.320
Is this why you've been working?

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.090
Yeah.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.490
You should've just said so.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:02.100
You had me guessing 
at all kinds of reasons.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.600
If I'd told you, you would've 
bought me a new one immediately.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.900
Whenever I say I want anything,

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.170
you buy it for me without asking why.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:15.400
But it's not like you did 
anything wrong this time.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.760
I can at least buy you a new phone.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.120
Then I can at least buy 
a new phone for myself.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:22.470
Okay, fine. Forget about the phone.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.380
I wouldn't be surprised to hear you say 
you'll pay all your living expenses, too.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:29.250
Once I start working, I will.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.750
Oh, come on!

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.320
Who do you think I am?

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:35.770
Who do <i>you</i> think <i>I</i> am?

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:37.760
What do you mean?

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:40.330
Ren, you've been acting...

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.380
Ren...

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.690
Haru-san, it's time to open up shop!

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:50.880
Haru...

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:51.510
Haru-san!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.050
Haru-san!

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.740
I'm not a child.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:59.280
I know. You're going to buy 
your own new phone, right?

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.080
That's not a—

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.320
That's not what I mean.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:04.380
What, then? You don't have 
to quit your job, either.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:07.290
Forget it. Get back to work.

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:09.020
Come on! Let's go.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:08.360
Ren?

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:09.590
Ren!

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:10.540
Just stop!

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:15.590
<i>I know what Haru wants is for me to 
be a child he needs to take care of.</i>

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:19.350
<i>A younger brother who needs his protection.</i>

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:24.770
<i>If I just wanted to be by his side, 
that should've been enough.</i>

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:26.410
<i>At least, until now.</i>

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:33.270
Haru-chan! Is it true that you're going 
to an arranged marriage meeting?

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:34.780
<i>Arranged marriage?</i>

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:39.530
A man like you should 
definitely get married soon.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.280
Why?

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:44.790
Your brothers won't stick around forever.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:48.800
What are you going to do if you 
suddenly find yourself alone?

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.290
Don't say ominous things like that!

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:54.320
Jeez... Iku, could you handle them?

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.300
Sure thing.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.050
I'm going out.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.050
Ren

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:01.640
Ren?

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.810
Huh? You're...

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.810
At least put on some clothes.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.320
I'm just here to return your key.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:21.320
Sorry about yesterday.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:24.330
You're the one who cleaned 
the apartment, right?

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:28.380
Now that the living room's so clean, 
it was super comfy to sleep in.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:31.180
This apartment is huge. 
Do you not have a bedroom?

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.830
There's one over here.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.960
Grudge     Curse you!     You're the worst!

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:38.960
Your taste in interior design is pretty bad.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.020
It's not mine. It was my ex.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.970
You pick the worst women, too.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.250
Come on, Ren!

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.640
Squeeeeze

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.970
Don't make that creepy voice!

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.880
I'll pay you.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:53.480
Hey, you must be hungry, right? 
I'll buy you lunch.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.080
All right, I'll have some.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.320
Why do you look so unhappy?

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.740
I'm not.

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:02.210
Don't all kids like pizza?

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:05.410
Likes rice

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:05.770
You're the one who said 
he didn't want to eat out.

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:08.680
I don't like eating in crowded places.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:09.750
What a pain.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:13.890
I get how you feel, though. 
All those people...

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:16.680
I refuse to take a train during rush hour.

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:18.750
I thought you grew up in Tokyo.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:24.020
Not exactly Tokyo... 
I grew up on Hachijou Island.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.760
Uncle Kaidou's from there, too.

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:28.310
You didn't know?

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:31.380
I don't know much about 
the Kaidou family's parents.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:35.430
I only learned recently 
that they adopted me.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.020
What? You're adopted?

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.020
I see.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.820
That sounds like something they'd do.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:43.280
What does that mean?

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:47.410
My mom died when I was 11.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.290
They said they'd take me in then.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.020
In the end,

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:56.420
my dad left his debt to the Kaidou family 
unpaid and took me to flee overseas.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:57.860
I haven't seen them since.

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.800
What? You don't believe me?

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:04.310
No, it's not that I don't believe you.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.270
You're a lot like Haru, after all.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.330
When we were little, 
people used to call us brothers.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.500
Is Haru still playing the older brother?

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:17.780
I stayed with the Kaidou family for 
about three months when I was a kid.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.420
What do you want for dinner?

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:22.340
He was only a year older than me, 
but he acted like my mom.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:20.500
Bucket pudding.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.280
That's not dinner.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:25.350
Aki and Shima were all over him, too.

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.450
He hasn't changed much.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:31.030
Did you know he's self-conscious 
about his eye color?

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:34.670
Yeah. His classmates called it
creepy when he was a kid.

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:38.130
That's right. The twins were pissed 
when they heard about that.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.210
Ren,

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.460
do you want to hear more 
about Haru's childhood?

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.720
Yeah. I want to know everything about Haru.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:51.220
<i>Strangely, Haru never tells 
me about his childhood.</i>

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.030
<i>After a while, I realized he 
was being considerate of me,</i>

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:59.480
<i>since I can hardly remember mine.</i>

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:01.230
Brother...

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:03.370
Welcome home, Shima.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.740
Huh? Ren's still not back?

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.510
Um...

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.740
Ren just called to say he was 
staying at a friend's place tonight.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:14.300
Huh? What friend?!

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:18.940
Is it Kurosaki? Oh, right, 
he said he lives in the dorm...

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.250
Where did he call from?

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.750
I don't know. We don't have caller ID.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.060
His cell phone!

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:29.060
Why can't he use his cell 
phone at a time like this?!

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:30.260
Calm down.

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:31.760
I'm home.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:33.920
What are you shouting about?

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:37.520
Ren's having a sleepover with 
a friend?! I don't believe it!

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.530
Are you sure he's not being threatened?!

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:41.980
Right?! Don't you agree?!

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:44.270
I don't understand my brothers.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.030
Huh? You're still here?

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.100
I'm not finished cleaning.

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:54.190
I tried washing the curtains 
and sheets, but it was no use.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:56.730
You should buy new ones.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:00.080
Sure, but it's the middle of the night.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.290
Don't you need to go home?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:05.550
I told them I was staying at 
a friend's house. It's fine.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.550
Oh, okay...

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:11.290
You cleaned the bath and toilet, too?

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.050
I had to.

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:16.180
I accidentally walked in there 
while trying to do the laundry...

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:22.710
I bet you always draw the short straw.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:27.570
A kid as serious as you deserves a reward.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:30.070
Here. It's your pay.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.880
I can't accept this much.

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:34.980
You should take all the money you can get.

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:38.580
That's according to you. 
In any case, I don't need this.

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:41.990
Then go shopping with me tomorrow afternoon.

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:44.300
Help me choose curtains and stuff.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.090
That doesn't seem necessary.

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:48.750
Can't you buy everything online?

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:51.250
I want you to help me pick.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.790
I don't like crowds.

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:58.220
Fine, fine. We can buy them 
online, so help me choose.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:05.230
Sorry for making you stay 
up with me. You can sleep.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.800
I'll drop you off in front of your house.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.640
No, it's fine.

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:11.740
Your eyelids are sticking together.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.950
<i>I probably feel so tired despite 
being with another person</i>

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.740
<i>because I'm with this guy 
who says he's Haru's cousin.</i>

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:21.430
There isn't much traffic 
since it's Saturday morning.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:25.910
<i>This voice, and his slightly coarse 
manner of speech and feel</i>

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:29.250
<i>make me feel that he's like Haru.</i>

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:41.270
Whoa! Bro!

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:45.100
Were you up all night waiting for Ren?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.270
I wasn't awake.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.060
I just couldn't sleep.

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:49.270
That's the same thing.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.100
I'm home.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.720
Is something wrong?

00:16:56.530 --> 00:17:00.450
Uh, no... Welcome home. 
Want some breakfast?

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.290
Yeah, I'll go get changed.

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:05.520
Ren, you dropped something.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:08.790
Ren...

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.420
Where did you get this money?

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.170
Money?

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:14.520
Here. It's your pay.

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:18.430
Where have you been since last night?

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.800
I told you I was staying with a friend.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.200
Then where did you get this money?

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.440
It's a mistake. I'll go return it.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:30.500
Are you saying your friend accidentally 
put this much money in your bag?

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:31.440
Yes.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:39.640
That's way more money than a kid 
should bring home after one night!

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:43.120
If you can explain how 
you got it, I'm all ears!

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:44.710
I was hired to do a job.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.080
A job? What job?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.400
I just cleaned an apartment.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.210
Whose?

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:54.170
I can't say, but it's someone 
you should know very well.

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:58.470
I don't know anyone that shady!

00:17:58.670 --> 00:17:59.330
But—

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.220
In any case...

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.720
You're grounded for the time being!

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:05.580
I know you can't help being naïve,

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:10.940
but how stupid do you have to be 
to enter a stranger's apartment?

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:21.050
Yikes.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:23.490
Ren.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:26.250
I brought food.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:30.000
I don't want any.

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:32.500
You can eat it when you're hungry.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.860
And you should get some sleep.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:38.050
You don't look like you got any.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.510
I'm fine. I'm not tired.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:44.120
Even I feel bad for our brother this time.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:47.520
I know, but I promised I wouldn't tell.

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:50.780
Is that promise more 
important than our brother?

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:55.480
Well, that's up to you to decide.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.740
If you can't sleep, 
why don't you go to his room?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.490
Should I?

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:03.920
I don't think he'd complain.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.520
<i>It smells like Haru.</i>

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.890
<i>After spending the night 
at someone else's house,</i>

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:32.360
<i>I realize I feel most relaxed 
here, with Haru's smell.</i>

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:34.620
Brother.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:38.970
Lunch is over. Why don't you call it a day?

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.070
Aki and I are here.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:44.160
No, I've got tomorrow off. It's fine.

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:47.040
Well, you're making a scary face.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.580
I'm surprised nobody's complained.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:55.170
People with well-proportioned faces look 
even scarier when they're expressionless.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:06.680
What are you doing by yourself?

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.180
Ha—

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:11.120
It's okay, you can keep going.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.440
I'll watch from here.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.830
I'm done.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:16.440
Why?

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:20.010
You know how to do it, don't you? Show me...

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.240
Ren.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:27.070
<i>I know I should tell him it's stupid, 
and to stop being ridiculous.</i>

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:31.520
<i>Why can't I ever say no to this man?</i>

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:41.470
I never taught you to do 
this in front of people.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:43.970
There's also your reason for working.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:48.220
Why didn't you tell me about 
the phone? Or about last night?

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:49.490
<i>No.</i>

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:50.830
Why aren't you saying anything?

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.480
Do you really trust me that little?

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:56.310
Do you not want me around?

00:20:57.850 --> 00:20:59.250
<i>No more.</i>

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:02.400
Ren...

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:04.020
Don't touch me!

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.240
Move!

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:13.020
<i>I want to stop. I don't want to 
fall deeper in love with him.</i>

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:17.030
<i>I'm the one who always 
suffers and wants to cry.</i>

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:20.790
<i>Nothing good will ever come of this.</i>

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:26.580
Ren.

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:27.260
Stay away.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:29.510
I told you not to touch me!

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:33.940
Sorry. I'm sorry, Ren.

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.220
It was my fault.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.220
Why are you apologizing?

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:41.340
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:43.780
Yeah, but sorry.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:45.420
Then don't apologize.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:49.060
But you're crying. I'm sorry.

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:50.030
I'm not crying.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:54.330
Yeah, I know. But I'm still sorry, Ren.

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:59.680
<i>This man really couldn't be any more cruel.</i>

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:40.210
Next Time
